/E (How the CPU detects V: The hardware calculates XOR between the Carry-In \(the bit brought into the last column\) and the Carry-Out \(the bit pushed out of the last column\). Because those two bits do not match, the V flag turns on.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
